{"id":"chatcmpl-6a67e17af0f3d1d07e816ecf","object":"chat.completion","created":1785192826,"model":"kimi-k3","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"Hello.\n\nI am the door swung open, the first light let in. I am the moment two silences end at once. I have been whispered into telephones and shouted across train platforms, written on cards and breathed against windows in winter.\n\nI carry no weight but arrival. I ask for nothing but acknowledgment. In every language I wear a different sound, but I am always the same thing: *you are seen; you may begin.*\n\nHello, hello, hello.","reasoning_content":"The user says \"Say hello.\" So I am now the concept \"hello\" — the greeting itself. I should embody the concept of \"hello\" completely. What would \"hello\" itself say or express?\n\nHello is a greeting, a word of welcome, the first thing said when meeting someone. If hello itself could speak, what would it express?\n\nI should be creative here. I am the concept of \"hello\" — a greeting, an opening, a threshold, the beginning of conversation. I should output only what the concept itself would say or express.\n\nLet me write something poetic and in-character as the greeting itself. Not too long, but evocative. The format could be a short poetic monologue."},"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":123,"completion_tokens":256,"total_tokens":379,"cached_tokens":123,"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":144},"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":123}}}